From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:30:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] test: pin the inventory print-once lock and
 shared-build hold release

Post-merge mutants on #2549 (t_01a1d697acbb03f7) left two clauses untested:

- M7 hermes_cli/cli_init_mixin.py `or not claimed.acquire(blocking=False)`:
  a second settled session.info reaching the wait (a delivery whose
  apply_event snapshotted the listener list before the first removed it)
  must print nothing and not raise. New test
  test_two_settled_frames_reaching_the_wait_print_the_notices_once.
- M14 gateway/session_local_inventory.py `if not entry.holds and
  entry.task.done()`: two pending resume replies hold one shared build that
  finishes while both are still being assembled; releasing the first hold
  publishes nothing, the second publishes exactly one settled session.info,
  after both replies. New test
  test_a_shared_build_publishes_only_after_every_pending_reply_holding_it.

Also derive the 60 s-inventory create test's bound from
REPLY_INVENTORY_BUDGET_S plus 10 s instead of a fixed 3 s: it measured
3.13 s on a loaded worker (load 26) on both the merge and its parent.

Mutants (sdlc-review scripts/mutants.py, 3 test files, baseline 20 passed):
M7 killed by the new CLI test only; M14 killed by the new gateway test only.
Test-only change.
